body:
I have 2 inherited-style models,
and when I create a new entity using repository.create(JSON),
it just skips the inherited fields.

These are my models

```
@Table()
@TableInheritance("class-table")
export class Document {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    id: number;
    @OneToMany(type => DocumentLine, documentLine => documentLine.document)
    documentLines: DocumentLine[];
    @Column()
    dollarRate: number = 0;
    @Column()
    orderBy: string = '';
    @Column()
    comments: string = '';
    @Column()
    subTotal: number = 0;
    @Column()
    vat: number = 0;
    @Column()
    total: number = 0;
    @Column()
    createdBy: string = '';
    @CreateDateColumn()
    createdAt: string;
    @UpdateDateColumn()
    updatedAt: string;
}
```

```
@ClassTableChild()
export class DeliveryNote extends Document {
    @ManyToOne(type => Customer, customer => customer.deliveryNotes)
    customer: Customer;
    @Column()
    invoice: string = '';
}
```

What can cause this?
I have used repository.create so far, and it's a good automatic way for converting the JSON into an entity. I don't want to manually insert the inherited fields now :)

Also, when will the [table inheritance page](https://typeorm.github.io/table-inheritance.html) be ready? It's hard for me to guess how to use them by the [samples](https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/tree/master/sample)
